WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.125
Scope is what keeps those roles narrow.

2
00:00:02.125 --> 00:00:04.571
Help desk roles are assigned over AUs,

3
00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:08.437
and at that scope they reach
only members with no admin role.

4
00:00:08.437 --> 00:00:12.756
Executives go further, into a
restricted unit that only a small,

5
00:00:12.756 --> 00:00:17.738
approved support group can touch; even
tenant-wide admins can't edit them.

6
00:00:17.738 --> 00:00:20.871
One caution: don't put the
technicians themselves in one,

7
00:00:20.871 --> 00:00:23.663
because governance features
stop working there.

8
00:00:23.663 --> 00:00:27.890
Roles reach technicians through one
group per role and scope, eligible

9
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:32.475
rather than active, and activated with
a justification that cites the ticket.

10
00:00:32.475 --> 00:00:35.000
Those groups also protect their members,

11
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.863
so one technician can't reset
another and inherit their access.

12
00:00:38.863 --> 00:00:41.760
Now, recovering someone
who's lost everything.
